  "body": "### Summary\nAs a contributor, I want `ReaderInsetsWebTests.aRestoreWhileHiddenDoesNotKeepTheControllerAlive()` to pass deterministically, so that unrelated PRs stop failing their required app job.\n\n### Facts (2026-11-10)\n- Failed in the app job of PR #761 (run 42902785467, attempt 2: the only failing test; the PR does not touch the reader insets) and earlier in PR #743 (run 42840450745) and PR #761 (run 42890094480), each time alongside or instead of #704's `MessageTitleToneTests`. Passes on rerun.\n- Same family as the closed #642 (another `ReaderInsetsWebTests` case): a real `WKWebView` test whose timing depends on the CI runner's load. It looks like a deallocation check after a restore while hidden; under load the controller may still be referenced when the check runs.\n\n### Scope\nFind what the test waits on (deallocation, a pending web-view callback), make it deterministic without only raising a timeout, and show 20 green runs under CPU load on a simulator (the #704 measurement method).\n\nRefs #704, #642.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
